<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">North Ossetia–Alania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as North Ossetia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetia">Ossetia</a>–Alania is a republic of the Russian Federation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a> on the Terek river. Most of its people are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>, an Iranian-speaking people descended from the medieval Alans, whose name the republic added to its official title in 1994. In 2004 the Beslan school siege took place there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-ossetia-alania.jpg" alt="North Ossetia–Alania" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nardo Polo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Ossetia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
